{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And they made him drink, etc.</b> Wine was made available to them in the cave, to bring forth from them two nations." "<b>And she lay with her father.</b> But concerning the younger it is written ״וַתִּשְׁכַּב עִמּוֹ״? The younger — because she did not initiate the harlotry but her sister taught her, Scripture spared her and did not specify her disgrace; but the elder, who initiated the harlotry, Scripture publicized explicitly." "<b>And when she arose.</b> Of the elder it is pointed [with a dagesh in the qof], to say that upon her arising he knew — and even so, he did not guard himself on the second night from drinking. Rabbi Levi said: Anyone who is ravenous after the bulmus of forbidden relations — in the end he is fed from his own flesh."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {2 "בולמוס (bulmus) is a Greek loanword (βολιμός, 'insatiable hunger'); retained as written."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:36.223068380Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}